      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "Given the fact that most people seem to think that any new environments which are introduced to the game should be as widely-applicable as possible (see here: http://greaterthangames.info/forum/index.php/topic,148.0.html), then how many of these generic environments (i.e. you can picture fighting just about any villain there) can we think up?\n\nKeep in mind that if any of these actually appear in future expansions, it's because the >Games guys had already thought them up, not that they got the idea from here, so their lawyers don't need to worry. :)\n\nI'll start:\n\n1) Underground Cave Complex\n - cave-ins\n - mole people\n - blind cave creatures\n - mysterious underground lake\n - lava flows\n - etc.\n\n2) Time Travel Vortex\n - mammoths\n - pirates\n - WWII soldiers\n - future cops\n - bi-planes\n - time swirls and chrono flows\n - etc.\n\n3) Arctic Base\n - whiteouts/snowblindness\n - frostbite\n - crevasses\n - avalanches\n - wendigo/yeti monsters\n - automated base defenses\n - various domes within the base (power, biodome, research, etc.)\n - etc.\n\n4) Area 51\n - all the zany alien stuff you'd expect to find in Area 51\n\nAnyone else got ideas?",
